 FIREBASE DEPLOYMENT CHECKLIST
Use this for EVERY new building deployment

STEP 1: CREATE FIREBASE PROJECT (2 min)

Go to: https://console.firebase.google.com
Click "Add project"
Project name: payment-[building-name] (e.g., payment-rothschild-12)
Disable Google Analytics (not needed)
Click "Create project"
Wait for completion → Click "Continue"


STEP 2: ENABLE REALTIME DATABASE (1 min)

Left sidebar → Click "Realtime Database"
Click "Create Database"
Location: Select "Europe (europe-west1)" (or your region)
Security rules: Select "Start in locked mode"
Click "Enable"
Wait for database creation


STEP 3: ENABLE AUTHENTICATION (1 min)

Left sidebar → Click "Authentication"
Click "Get started"
Click "Sign-in method" tab
Find "Email/Password" row
Click on it
Toggle "Enable" to ON
Click "Save"


STEP 4: ADD AUTHORIZED DOMAIN (30 sec)

Still in Authentication section
Click "Settings" tab (top of page)
Scroll down to "Authorized domains" section
Click "Add domain"
Enter: valerykg.github.io (or your custom domain)
Click "Add"


STEP 5: GET FIREBASE CONFIG (1 min)

Click ⚙️ icon (top left) → Select "Project settings"
Scroll down to "Your apps" section
Click "</>" icon (Web app)
App nickname: payment-tracker
DO NOT check Firebase Hosting checkbox
Click "Register app"
COPY the entire firebaseConfig object:

javascriptconst firebaseConfig = {
  apiKey: "...",
  authDomain: "...",
  projectId: "...",
  databaseURL: "...",
  storageBucket: "...",
  messagingSenderId: "...",
  appId: "..."
};

Click "Continue to console"


STEP 6: UPDATE HTML FILE (2 min)

Open your HTML file in text editor
Find line ~27 with old firebaseConfig
REPLACE entire firebaseConfig object with the one you copied
IMPORTANT: Keep this line AFTER the config:

javascript   firebase.initializeApp(firebaseConfig);

Save file


STEP 7: CREATE FIRST ADMIN USER (3 min)
A. Create user in Authentication:

Firebase Console → Authentication → Users tab
Click "Add user" button
Email: admin@test.com (or your preferred admin email)
Password: Choose strong password (min 6 characters)
Click "Add user"
COPY THE UID - long string like K3B96KicLke8PiwnyeG7hWwzjfO2

(Click on user row to see full UID if needed)



B. Add admin role in Database:
METHOD 1: Import JSON (Faster)

Firebase Console → Realtime Database → Data tab
Click "⋮" (three dots menu) at top right
Select "Import JSON"
Paste this JSON (replace YOUR_UID_HERE with copied UID):

json{
  "users": {
    "YOUR_UID_HERE": {
      "role": "admin",
      "username": "admin",
      "email": "admin@test.com",
      "createdAt": "2025-11-03T10:00:00Z"
    }
  }
}

Click "Import"
for manager - 
{
  "users": {
    "MANAGER_UID_HERE": {
      "role": "manager",
      "username": "manager",
      "email": "manager@test.com",
      "createdAt": "2025-11-03T16:30:00Z"
    }
  }
}


METHOD 2: Manual Entry (Slower)

Firebase Console → Realtime Database → Data tab
Hover over root / → Click "+"
Name: users → Click "+" next to it
Name: [PASTE YOUR UID] → Click "+" next to it
Add these 4 fields:

Name: role → Value: admin
Name: username → Value: admin
Name: email → Value: admin@test.com
Name: createdAt → Value: 2025-11-03T10:00:00Z


Click "Add"


STEP 8: SET FIREBASE SECURITY RULES (2 min)

Firebase Console → Realtime Database → Rules tab
DELETE ALL existing rules
COPY-PASTE these rules exactly:

json{
  "rules": {
    "buildingData": {
      ".read": "auth != null",
      ".write": "auth != null && (root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('role').val() === 'admin' || root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('role').val() === 'manager')",
      "buildingSettings": {
        "privacyOptOuts": {
          "$apartmentNum": {
            ".write": "auth != null && root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('apartmentNumber').val() == $apartmentNum"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "users": {
      ".read": "auth != null && (root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('role').val() === 'admin' || root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('role').val() === 'manager')",
      "$uid": {
        ".read": "auth != null && (auth.uid === $uid || root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('role').val() === 'admin' || root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('role').val() === 'manager')",
        ".write": "auth != null && (root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('role').val() === 'admin' || (root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('role').val() === 'manager' && (!newData.exists() || newData.child('role').val() === 'resident')))"
      }
    },
    "supportBackups": {
      ".read": "auth != null && root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('role').val() === 'admin'",
      ".write": "auth != null && root.child('users').child(auth.uid).child('role').val() === 'admin'"
    }
  }
}

Click "Publish"
Confirm warning dialog


STEP 9: DEPLOY TO GITHUB PAGES (3 min)

Save your updated HTML file
Commit to GitHub:

bash   git add index.html
   git commit -m "Update Firebase config for new deployment"
   git push origin main

Wait 1-2 minutes for GitHub Pages to rebuild
Visit: https://valerykg.github.io/payment/


STEP 10: TEST DEPLOYMENT (2 min)

Open deployed URL in browser
Login as admin:

Username: admin@test.com (or your email)
Password: [your chosen password]


Should see "Admin Panel" button
Click Admin Panel → Try creating a test project
Check Firebase Database → Should see buildingData node created


✅ DEPLOYMENT COMPLETE
Total time: ~15 minutes

📋 QUICK CHECKLIST

☐ Firebase project created
☐ Realtime Database enabled (Europe region)
☐ Authentication enabled (Email/Password)
☐ Authorized domain added
☐ Firebase config copied to HTML
☐ Admin user created in Auth
☐ Admin role added to Database
☐ Security rules published
☐ HTML pushed to GitHub
☐ Login tested successfully


🔧 TROUBLESHOOTING
Can't login:

Check UID matches between Auth and Database
Verify Firebase rules are published
Clear browser cache

Database not connecting:

Verify databaseURL in config is correct
Check authorized domains include your deployment URL
Check browser console for errors

Permission denied:

Verify user has role: "admin" in database
Re-publish Firebase rules
Re-login


END OF GUIDE



